### BUG-01 · Footer permanently hidden behind Mobile Bottom Nav on iOS
| | |
|---|---|
| **Severity** | 🔴 Critical |
| **Type** | Spacing / Safe-Area Overlap |
| **Files** | [`App.tsx`](file:///c:/Users/agawa/OneDrive/Documents/ChatGPT/Fly%20Rc%20Project/torque-rc-store/src/App.tsx#L89) · [`MobileBottomNav.tsx`](file:///c:/Users/agawa/OneDrive/Documents/ChatGPT/Fly%20Rc%20Project/torque-rc-store/src/components/layout/MobileBottomNav.tsx#L23) |
| **Lines** | `App.tsx:89` — `pb-16` · `MobileBottomNav.tsx:23` — `h-16` + `pb-safe` |

**Root Cause:** The root wrapper (`App.tsx:89`) reserves `pb-16` (64px) for the fixed bottom nav. But the nav (`MobileBottomNav.tsx:23`) also adds `pb-safe` for the iPhone home indicator, making the bar **taller** than 64px. The footer's bottom portion is permanently clipped.

**Fix:**
```diff
 // App.tsx:89
-<div className="min-h-screen bg-background flex flex-col pb-16 lg:pb-0">
+<div className="min-h-screen bg-background flex flex-col pb-[calc(4rem+env(safe-area-inset-bottom))] lg:pb-0">
```

