### BUG-14 · Product Detail: Tab buttons not interactive (non-functional tabs)
| | |
|---|---|
| **Severity** | 🟡 Medium |
| **Type** | UX / Missing State |
| **File** | [`ProductDetailPage.tsx`](file:///c:/Users/agawa/OneDrive/Documents/ChatGPT/Fly%20Rc%20Project/torque-rc-store/src/pages/ProductDetailPage.tsx#L205-L207) |
| **Lines** | `:205-207` |

**Root Cause:** The three tab buttons ("Product Overview", "Technical Details", "In the Box") are statically rendered. Only "Product Overview" has the active `border-accent` underline — there's no `useState` tab-switching logic. Clicking the other two tabs does nothing, confusing users.

**Fix:** Add tab state management:
```diff
 // ProductDetailPage.tsx — add state at top of component (around Line 10)
+const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState('overview');

 // ProductDetailPage.tsx:205-207 — replace static buttons with dynamic
-<button className="... border-b-2 border-accent ...">Product Overview</button>
-<button className="... border-b-2 border-transparent ...">Technical Details</button>
-<button className="... border-b-2 border-transparent ...">In the Box</button>
+<button onClick={() => setActiveTab('overview')} className={cn("... pb-4 border-b-2", activeTab === 'overview' ? 'border-accent text-white' : 'border-transparent text-muted-foreground hover:text-white')}>Product Overview</button>
+<button onClick={() => setActiveTab('specs')} className={cn("... pb-4 border-b-2", activeTab === 'specs' ? 'border-accent text-white' : 'border-transparent text-muted-foreground hover:text-white')}>Technical Details</button>
+<button onClick={() => setActiveTab('inbox')} className={cn("... pb-4 border-b-2", activeTab === 'inbox' ? 'border-accent text-white' : 'border-transparent text-muted-foreground hover:text-white')}>In the Box</button>
```
Then conditionally render tab content below based on `activeTab`.

