### BUG-15 · Hero: Image path uses `/src/assets/` — will break in production build
| | |
|---|---|
| **Severity** | 🟡 Medium |
| **Type** | Asset Path / Build Error |
| **Files** | [`Hero.tsx`](file:///c:/Users/agawa/OneDrive/Documents/ChatGPT/Fly%20Rc%20Project/torque-rc-store/src/components/home/Hero.tsx#L14) · [`CategoryShowcase.tsx`](file:///c:/Users/agawa/OneDrive/Documents/ChatGPT/Fly%20Rc%20Project/torque-rc-store/src/components/home/CategoryShowcase.tsx#L10-L40) |
| **Lines** | `Hero.tsx:14` · `CategoryShowcase.tsx:10,16,22,28,34,40` |

**Root Cause:** Images reference `/src/assets/images/...` as string paths. Vite's dev server serves `/src/` directly, so this works in dev. But after `vite build`, the `/src/` directory doesn't exist in the output — **all hero and category images will 404 in production**.

**Fix:** Import images as ES modules so Vite can hash and bundle them:
```diff
 // Hero.tsx — top of file
+import heroImage from '../../assets/images/hero_rc_car_cinematic_1790434394611.jpg';

 // Hero.tsx:14
-src="/src/assets/images/hero_rc_car_cinematic_1790434394611.jpg"
+src={heroImage}
```
Same pattern for all 6 images in `CategoryShowcase.tsx`.

